+--[[ v2.61 (ground): the garden islands are deeper UNDER the yard. The island's underside is a stack of 4-stud layers
+	(each narrower than the one above); the pit digs down to BlockConfig.Below slots, so the layer whose bottom is at
+	`wideBottom` (the widest rock layer: it holds the whole 100x100 yard) is stretched down by `delta` studs and
+	every layer under it moves down by `delta`. DeepenBox(bottom, delta, wideBottom) -> dy (move the part's centre),
+	dh (grow its height): the part is not touched when it lies above the wide layer. ]]
+BlockMath.IslandWideBottom = -10
+-- v2.61: a ray (plot-local origin o, direction d) that flew down an open pit and left through the BOTTOM (Trace's `place` is then
