+	Twice a second (BlockService.Start) the server compares the characters with the DATA of the blocks
+	(the truth the bricks are built from):
+	  • HEAL     a brick of a layer that was destroyed from outside (a script that cleared the plot, a
+	             part streamed out and lost …) makes its layer rebuild (before: it stayed gone until
+	             somebody changed that layer)
+	  • NOCLIP   the middle of a character is INSIDE a solid block of the data (the client does not
+	             have / does not collide with the bricks, tunnelled, a hole was filled around it) for
+	             two checks in a row: it is put on the first free spot above, in the middle of its cell
+	  • PIT      somebody stands idle (no swing, no block, no step) deeper than two blocks in a pit for
+	             20 s (there is no jumping out of a 20-stud shaft): lifted back to the garden's spawn
